1.19.9999 (development)
  * Bootstrap operations can run in parallel with the new 'cl' argument (issue #46)
  * Restored progress bars in bootstrap operations; 'progress' is no longer deprecated
  * The deprecated 'parallel' argument now warns as the documentation stated
  * Fixed 'ci.coords' returning fractions instead of percentages on 'percent=TRUE' curves
  * Fixed 'cov' and 'roc.test' dropping a whole curve instead of the replicate on NA bootstrap values
  * Fixed 'ci.coords' on smoothed curves, which failed unless 'input' was given explicitly
  * 'ci.coords' now rejects input="threshold" on smoothed curves, as 'coords' does
  * Added tests for bootstrap operations (issue #28)
  * Added base graphics add-on functions 'polygon_auc', 'polygon_max_auc',
    'polygon_ci' and 'text' methods for 'auc', 'ci.auc', 'roc' and
    'smooth.roc', and 'panel.first'/'panel.last' arguments to 'plot.roc',
    so the auc.polygon/max.auc.polygon/print.auc appearance of 'plot.roc'
    can be built from separate roc(), auc() and ci() calls instead of
    one-shot arguments (issue #70). 'polygon_ci' always draws with
    'no.roc=TRUE', so unlike 'plot.ci(type="shape")' it never redraws the
    curve and never loses a customized col/lwd. Also fixes 'plot.roc'
    drawing the AUC/CI label twice when both 'ci=TRUE' and
    'print.auc=TRUE' were used, and 'text()'/'plot.ci.se'/'plot.ci.sp'/
    'plot.ci.thresholds'/'plot.ci.coords' now give a clear error (instead
    of a low-level graphics one, or none at all for 'multiclass.auc') when
    called with no plot open or on a 'multiclass.auc' object.
  * Ordered predictors are no longer converted to numeric (issue #63).
    Thresholds are the levels plus an Inf sentinel; pass those labels
    (not numbers) to coords(), ci.thresholds(), ci.coords() and
    plot.roc(print.thres). ci.coords() omits the threshold interval by
    default on ordered curves. Its new default best.policy="unique.stop"
    merges "best" thresholds that are identical in all the returned
    values (such as empty levels) before stopping.
  * ci.coords() with best.policy="omit" now drops a bootstrap replicate
    that has several "best" points, instead of returning the first
    column of the coords data.frame.
  * Added ggplot2 layers for 'plot.roc' features on a 'ggroc' plot:
    'geom_polygon_auc', 'geom_polygon_max_auc', 'geom_roc_identity',
    'geom_text_auc', 'geom_roc_threshold', 'geom_polygon_ci', and
    'geom_errorbar_ci' (issue #129)
  * Documented the justification of the stratified bootstrap (issue #131).
  * Fixed 'power.roc.test' with two partial AUC curves failing with
    "DeLong method is not supported for partial AUC" instead of
    defaulting to bootstrap when 'method' was not given.
  * Fixed error when 'ggroc' received a mixed list of empirical and smoothed ROC curves
  * 'ggroc' now sets Specificity/Sensitivity axis labels like 'plot.roc'
  * 'ggroc' now uses 'coord_fixed()' like 'plot.roc(asp = 1)'. Add another
    coordinate system (for example 'coord_cartesian()') to replace it.
  * Added a ggplot2 screenshot gallery vignette
  * 'size' is deprecated in 'ggroc' and the ggplot2 line and polygon layers in favour of 'linewidth'
  * Fixed the confidence interval of the paired DeLong 'roc.test' being on the 0-1 scale for 'percent=TRUE' curves
  * 'roc.test' now checks 'conf.level' also when the method is selected automatically
  * Fixed 'roc.test' and 'cov' ignoring the partial AUC of 'auc' objects of smoothed curves
  * 'roc.test', 'cov' and 'var' now give the documented error on curves smoothed with numeric 'density.controls' and 'density.cases' instead of D=Inf or 0
  * Fixed the mixing proportion of the unpaired Venkatraman test when the two curves have different numbers of observations
  * Fixed 'multiclass.roc' with a predictor matrix failing with 'Could not find any decision values' when exactly half of the response levels had no matching column
  * Fixed 'multiclass.roc' failing with 'No case observation.' when 'levels' contained a level without observations in a non-factor response, or that was not a level of the factor; it is now dropped with a warning as for unused factor levels
  * Fixed a false 'The following classes were not found in 'response'' warning in 'multiclass.roc' with a predictor matrix and a subset of 'levels'
  * Fixed 'power.roc.test' with 'method="bootstrap"', which computed the variance of each AUC from the wrong margin of the bootstrap replicates, giving essentially random results
  * Fixed 'power.roc.test' with two paired ROC curves with NAs at different positions, which failed or computed the power on misaligned observations
  * Fixed 'cov(method="obuchowski")' returning NaN for 'percent=TRUE' curves with a partial AUC
  * The 'var(method="obuchowski")' errors no longer claim to use the bootstrap instead
  * Fixed 'cov' failing or returning a wrong value for paired curves with NA values at different positions
  * 'roc.test' now gives the 'Missing argument predictor2' error also when 'predictor2 = NULL' is passed explicitly
  * Fixed 'roc.test' and 'cov' selecting DeLong (and failing) when only the second curve had a partial AUC
  * Curves built with the formula interface are now recognized as paired with curves built from the same data with the default interface, or with formula curves on data with different row names, so that `roc.test` and `cov` use the paired test.
  * `roc` with a formula or a data frame, `roc_` and `plot.roc` now return `NA` (or `NaN`) like the default interface when the data contains `NA` values with `na.rm = FALSE` (or infinite predictor values), instead of a malformed list.
  * `roc` with `density.controls` and `density.cases` now resolves `direction = "auto"` also when `auc = FALSE` (the curve could be inverted), and stores the resolved direction instead of `"auto"`.
  * `are.paired` and `roc.test` are no longer affected by objects named `oroc1` or `oroc2` in the user's workspace.
  * `are.paired(return.paired.rocs = TRUE)` now returns smoothed curves when given smoothed curves without missing values, and keeps the (partial) AUC and CI specification of smoothed curves.
  * `has.partial.auc` now checks that the `partial.auc` specification has length 2.
  * The warning for a deprecated `algorithm` argument now shows the value given instead of a literal `%s`.
  * Formula methods now give clear error messages for formulas without a response or with unsupported terms (such as `. - z` or interactions) instead of an internal `stopifnot` error.

1.19.1 (2026-08-27)
  * Added a FAQ vignette
  * Removed unused 'tcltk' from Suggests
  * Tests now skip if Suggest'ed packages are missing
  * Fix CRAN checks NOTE about 'structure()' special names ('.Names', '.Dim', '.Dimnames')

